{
  "info": {
    "name": "Myflix API (Supabase)",
    "description": "Calls the Myflix Supabase project the same way the app does, with email + password accounts.\n\n1. Select the **Myflix (Supabase)** environment. It needs `baseUrl` (no /rest/v1), `apiKey` (publishable key), and two test accounts: `nameA`, `emailA`, `passwordA`, `nameB`, `emailB`, `passwordB`.\n2. Run **Auth** first: it registers both accounts (or finds them) and logs in. A's token goes in `accessToken`, B's in `tokenB`.\n3. Every other folder runs as A, so row-level security applies: you only see and change A's rows.\n4. **Security checks** logs in as B and tries to read and change A's rows. Every request has tests; use **Run collection** to see them all pass.\n\nSupabase only accepts real email domains (not example.com). Gmail's + trick gives you two accounts from one inbox.\n\nSchema: supabase/schema.sql · docs/SCHEMA.md",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Supabase needs the project's publishable key on every request.",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'apikey', value: pm.environment.get('apiKey') });"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth (email + password)",
      "description": "Run these first. Log in as A saves accessToken (used by every folder below) and Log in as B saves tokenB (used by Security checks).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register account A",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/signup",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"email\": \"{{emailA}}\", \"password\": \"{{passwordA}}\", \"data\": { \"name\": \"{{nameA}}\" } }"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Same as the app's Register page: email + password, and the name goes into the account's metadata (the database trigger copies it into profiles). Uses emailA / passwordA / nameA from the environment."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// 200 = new account. 422 = this email already has an account, which is fine: log in next.",
                  "pm.test('account exists', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 422]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 422) pm.test('only because it already exists', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error_code).to.be.oneOf(['user_already_exists', 'email_exists']));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register account B",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/signup",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"email\": \"{{emailB}}\", \"password\": \"{{passwordB}}\", \"data\": { \"name\": \"{{nameB}}\" } }"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Same as the app's Register page: email + password, and the name goes into the account's metadata (the database trigger copies it into profiles). Uses emailB / passwordB / nameB from the environment."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// 200 = new account. 422 = this email already has an account, which is fine: log in next.",
                  "pm.test('account exists', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 422]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 422) pm.test('only because it already exists', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error_code).to.be.oneOf(['user_already_exists', 'email_exists']));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in as A",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"email\": \"{{emailA}}\", \"password\": \"{{passwordA}}\" }"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('userId', body.user.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('userIdA', body.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in as B",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"email\": \"{{emailB}}\", \"password\": \"{{passwordB}}\" }"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('tokenB', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('userIdB', body.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Wrong password is refused (400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"email\": \"{{emailA}}\", \"password\": \"not-the-password\" }"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Supabase never says whether the email or the password was wrong, so nobody can use it to find out who has an account."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('refused', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('same answer for wrong email or wrong password', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error_code).to.eql('invalid_credentials'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('refreshed', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"refresh_token\": \"{{refreshToken}}\" }"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/token?grant_type=refresh_token",
            "description": "Access tokens expire after an hour. Run this to get a new one without creating a new user."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/v1/user"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Catalog (logged-in users)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List shows with genre",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/shows?select=id,title,kind,release_year,seasons,maturity_rating,genres(name)&order=title"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List genres",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/genres?select=*&order=name"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Try to add a catalog show (blocked by RLS)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('catalog is read-only (403)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"id\": \"not-allowed\", \"title\": \"Not allowed\", \"release_year\": 2026, \"maturity_rating\": \"TV-14\", \"genre_id\": 1, \"created_by\": null}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/shows",
            "description": "Expected to fail with 403: catalog rows (created_by null) can only be added through migrations. Your own titles work: see Your titles & lists → Add my own movie."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Profile",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get my profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?select=*"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update display name",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Prefer",
                "value": "return=representation"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"display_name\": \"{{nameA}}\", \"avatar_color\": \"#46d369\" }"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?id=eq.{{userId}}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "My List",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get my list (with show titles and comments)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/list_entries?select=show_id,status,rating,added_at,updated_at,shows(title),list_comments(id,body,spoiler,created_at)&order=added_at.desc"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add a show",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Prefer",
                "value": "return=representation,resolution=merge-duplicates"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"show_id\": \"arcane\", \"status\": \"want\" }"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/list_entries?on_conflict=user_id,show_id",
            "description": "No user_id in the body: the database fills it in from your token (default auth.uid()). show_id must exist in shows."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('saved', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
                  "pm.test('owner filled in from the token', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()[0].user_id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('userIdA')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Rate a show",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Prefer",
                "value": "return=representation"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{ \"rating\": 5, \"status\": \"finished\" }"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/list_entries?show_id=eq.arcane"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
